The Concept: Building a complete distribution chart (histogram) of user behavior that explicitly includes the "zeroes"—making sure empty data categories don't just disappear from the final report.
Skills Used: Data Scaffolding, Recursive CTEs (WITH RECURSIVE), LEFT JOIN operations, Data Imputation (IFNULL).

Engineered a "Data Scaffolding" SQL architecture using a Recursive CTE to dynamically generate a continuous number sequence from zero up to the maximum data point.
Merged sparse, real-world user activity logs with the generated number sequence using LEFT JOINs to guarantee gapless, continuous reporting.
Built a comprehensive frequency chart that accurately exposed hidden "zero-activity" metrics (such as users who visited but made zero transactions) for complete business analytics.
